<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/O43286">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 5</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_B4GALT5_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_O43286" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B4GT5_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LacCer synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.274</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Lactosylceramide synthase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UDP-Gal:beta-GlcNAc beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,4-GalT II</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">b4Gal-T5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta-1,4-GalTase 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.-</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Beta4Gal-T5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glucosylceramide beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UDP-galactose:beta-N-acetylglucosamine beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B4GALT5</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference105623</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the synthesis of lactosylceramide (LacCer) viathe transfer of galactose from UDP-galactose to glucosylceramide(GlcCer) (PubMed:24498430). LacCer is the starting point in thebiosynthesis of all gangliosides (membrane-boundglycosphingolipids) which play pivotal roles in the CNS includingneuronal maturation and axonal and myelin formation (Bysimilarity). Plays a role in the glycosylation of BMPR1A andregulation of its protein stability (By similarity). Essential forextraembryonic development during early embryogenesis (Bysimilarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q9JMK0,ECO:0000269|PubMed:24498430}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=a beta-D-glucosyl-(1&lt;-&gt;1&apos;)-N-acylsphing-4-enine + UDP-alpha-D-galactose = beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;4)-beta-D-glucosyl-(1&lt;-&gt;1)-ceramide(d18:1(4E)) + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:31495,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:17950, ChEBI:CHEBI:22801,ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:66914; EC=2.4.1.274;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:24498430};COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035;Evidence={ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q9UBX8};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.PATHWAY: Sphingolipid metabolism.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus, Golgi stack membrane{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15291}; Single-pass type II membraneprotein. Golgi apparatus {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:A0A1S6M251}.Note=Trans cisternae of Golgi stack.{ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15291}.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Ubiquitously expressed.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:9435216}.INDUCTION: Up-regulated in subcutaneous adipose tissue duringobesity and diabetes. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:29415997}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 7 family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase;Note=Beta-1,4-galactosyltransferase 5;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_440&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">B4GT5_HUMAN Reviewed; 388 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_9334</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_004767</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_9334</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

