 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q9P109" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCNT4_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Core 2-branching enzyme 3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">C2GnT3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCNT4</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Core2-GlcNAc-transferase 3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.4.1.102</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference125644</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Glycosyltransferase that mediates core 2 O-glycanbranching, an important step in mucin-type biosynthesis. Does nothave core 4 O-glycan or I-branching enzyme activity.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10753916}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=O(3)-[beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-N-acetyl-alpha-D-galactosaminyl]-L-seryl-[protein] + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = 3-O-{beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;6)]-N-acetyl-alpha-D-galactosaminyl}-L-seryl-[protein] + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:56212, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:13922, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14419, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57705, ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:137949,ChEBI:CHEBI:139605; EC=2.4.1.102;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10753916};CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=O(3)-[beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-N-acetyl-alpha-D-galactosaminyl]-L-threonyl-[protein] + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = 3-O-{beta-D-galactosyl-(1-&gt;3)-[N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl-(1-&gt;6)]-N-acetyl-alpha-D-galactosaminyl}-L-threonyl-[protein] + H(+) + UDP; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:56216,Rhea:RHEA-COMP:13923, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14420, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:57705, ChEBI:CHEBI:58223, ChEBI:CHEBI:137950,ChEBI:CHEBI:139607; EC=2.4.1.102;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:10753916};PATHWAY: Protein modification; protein glycosylation.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Golgi apparatus membrane {ECO:0000250};Single-pass type II membrane protein {ECO:0000250}.TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Predominantly expressed in thymus. Weaklyexpressed in pancreas, peripheral blood leukocytes, placenta,small intestine and stomach. Barely detectable in liver, spleen,lung and lymph node. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10753916}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the glycosyltransferase 14 family.{ECO:0000305}.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Functional Glycomics Gateway - GTase; Note=Core2 beta-1,6-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase 3;URL=&quot;http://www.functionalglycomics.org/glycomics/molecule/jsp/glycoEnzyme/viewGlycoEnzyme.jsp?gbpId=gt_hum_542&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_51301</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GCNT4_HUMAN Reviewed; 453 AA.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

